fields.description:
Release policy built into the instance. Reads the value of PARA_GCM_REL_POLICY.

Usage: Read before selecting aesgcm_cfg.gcm_pass for decryption.

Values:
0x0 policy A only, verify then decrypt (reset value);
0x1 policy C only, release and flag;
0x2 both selectable;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

GHASH architecture of the instance. Reads the value of PARA_GHASH_ARCH.

Usage: Read to estimate the GCM throughput.

Values:
0x0 digit-serial;
0x1 single parallel multiplier (reset value);
0x2 aggregated parallel multipliers;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

AXI4 data width code of the data window. Reads the code of PARA_AXI_DATA_W.

Usage: Read before programming the DMA controller beat size.

Values:
0x0 32 bit (reset value);
0x1 64 bit;
0x2 128 bit;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Cipher mode. Selects ECB, CBC, CFB, OFB, CTR or GCM for the next message.

Usage: Program before start; use 0x5 only when aesgcm_cap.gcm_en reads 1.

Values:
0x0 ECB (reset value);
0x1 CBC;
0x2 CFB;
0x3 OFB;
0x4 CTR;
0x5 GCM;
0x6 to 0x7 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: Values 0x6 and 0x7 raise the configuration error event.

GCM pass. Selects single-pass processing or the pass of the verify-then-decrypt policy.

Usage: Program before start in GCM mode: 0x0 for encryption or policy C decryption, 0x1 for pass 1, 0x2 for pass 2 after aesgcm_sts.ver_ok reads 1.

Values:
0x0 single pass (reset value);
0x1 policy A pass 1, verify only;
0x2 policy A pass 2, decrypt;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: 0x1 and 0x2 require decryption; 0x0 with decryption requires policy C and aesgcm_sts.sec_only equal to 0.

CFB segment size code. Selects the CFB segment size for mode 2.

Usage: Program before start when aesgcm_cfg.mode equals 2.

Values:
0x0 1 bit (reset value);
0x1 2 bits;
0x2 4 bits;
0x3 8 bits;
0x4 16 bits;
0x5 32 bits;
0x6 64 bits;
0x7 128 bits;
0x8 to 0xF reserved.

Unit: bit.

Limits: 0x8 to 0xF raise the configuration error event.

GCM tag length code. Selects the number of leading tag bits that are produced or compared.

Usage: Program before start in GCM mode; the value is latched at aesgcm_ctrl.key_new and shall not change for the same key.

Values:
0x0 128 bits (reset value);
0x1 120 bits;
0x2 112 bits;
0x3 104 bits;
0x4 96 bits;
0x5 to 0x7 reserved.

Unit: bit.

Limits: 0x5 to 0x7 raise the configuration error event.

Sequencer phase. Encoded state of the message sequencer for diagnostics.

Usage: Read for debugging only; the encoding follows the state order of section 10.1.

Values:
0x0 idle (reset value);
0x1 to 0xD other states;
0xE aborting;
0xF reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

First error code of the last message. Identifies the first error that ended or rejected the message.

Usage: Read after an error event; cleared at the next start.

Values:
0x0 none (reset value);
0x1 CFG_ERR;
0x2 LEN_ERR;
0x3 CTR_EXHAUST;
0x4 KEY_ERR;
0x5 PROTO_ERR;
0x6 TAG_FAIL;
0x7 AES core error;
0x8 to 0xF reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Input burst size code. Number of beats of one input DMA burst.

Usage: Program before enabling the channel; must fit in the input FIFO.

Values:
0x0 1 beat (reset value);
0x1 2 beats;
0x2 4 beats;
0x3 8 beats;
0x4 16 beats;
0x5 to 0x7 reserved.

Unit: beat.

Limits: Burst bytes shall not exceed the FIFO capacity.

Output burst size code. Number of beats of one output DMA burst.

Usage: Program before enabling the channel.

Values:
0x0 1 beat (reset value);
0x1 2 beats;
0x2 4 beats;
0x3 8 beats;
0x4 16 beats;
0x5 to 0x7 reserved.

Unit: beat.

Limits: Burst bytes shall not exceed the FIFO capacity.
